      "lineNbr": 1717,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-31T14:14:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This feels too loose now. This would allow you to put other instructions in a root block that would be invalid, e.g.\n\n```\n%v:array\u003cu32\u003e \u003d var\u003cstorage\u003e\n%1 \u003d call arrayLength(%v)\n%2:u32 \u003d var\u003cprivate\u003e %1\n```\n\nThe `arrayLength` call is only used in the root block, but this should still not be allowed.\n\nI think we should be specifically checking for all the types of instructions that are allowed (`binary`, `unary`, `call`, `construct`, `convert`), and checking that their operands are all constants or other overrides (and also that they are only used in the root block).",
      "revId": "3be3786dfbc727256c507df57a7e00a6427e0e84",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75cd7444_1ae0e600",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/validator.cc",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 1717,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-31T23:47:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can, but is it worth it? We\u0027ll be removing this capabilty pretty eary in the pipeline, at which point any of those things (arrayLength, non-const value) would get caught immediately. So, is it worth it making this a lot more complicated?",
      "parentUuid": "caed0e45_2a03c9dc",
      "revId": "3be3786dfbc727256c507df57a7e00a6427e0e84",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1dc9bc7d_b1171cef",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/validator.cc",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 1717,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-01T01:58:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027ll likely be necessary to have this extra validation at some point, as the fuzzers will probably do this as soon as we add override support to the IR proto, and then break the `SubstituteOverrides` transform.\n\nWe can do it in a later date, but I wanted to call it out as a potential issue that we will likely hit later.",
      "parentUuid": "75cd7444_1ae0e600",
      "revId": "3be3786dfbc727256c507df57a7e00a6427e0e84",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
